      "image": "/infographics/03-hn-49863600.jpg",
      "content": "Formal specifications are finding unexpected practical utility in agentic software engineering. While traditional software development often treats formal methods like TLA+ and Lean as academic curiosities, integrating them into automated coding harnesses creates an immediate feedback loop for verifying correctness.\n\nTLA+ allows engineers to model distributed state transitions and critical invariants concisely before writing code. When combined with modern frontier models, the specification acts as an unambiguous constraint boundary. Instead of relying solely on probabilistic unit tests, the agent uses the model checker to explore edge cases and exhaustively eliminate race conditions.\n\nThis combination shifts agentic workflows from blind code generation toward formal synthesis and verification. Defining temporal properties upfront turns out to be the exact scaffolding needed to keep autonomous agents on track in complex architectures."
